Expected elements: present

Presence check first. Identity bar spans the full width at y0–60 and carries `← aztec` (chain exit — correct), the truncated hash, `Partial`, `block 101`, both stepping directions, a scrubber track at x672–833 with a cyan fill and thumb, the readout `128 / 1315` at x866–938 as a separate element, and the three-phase rail. Scrubber and readout are both present and unclipped at 1440. Below: one row of three columns — Code (x5–685), the `CALL TRACE | EVENT LOG` tab region over `VALUES` (x690–1145), and `TRANSACTION` (x1150–1435). Call Trace is the open tab; Values is a pane below the strip, not a third tab. No band above the panes, no full-width pane row, no page scrollbar.

The column split is sound; the vertical split inside the middle column is not. The tab region takes 492px of the column's 827px and 233px of it — 47% — is empty below `By call order.`, while the Values pane below it takes 327px, ends 33px from the bottom and has already had to wrap `masses` onto two lines. The height sits in the region that does not want it.

The Code pane clips six lines mid-token at its right edge with no scrollbar, fade or ellipsis, and clips line 52 to half height at its bottom edge. Inline value badges land on four different x positions with no anchor.

Fixes: give the tab region content height and the surplus to Values; give the code edge an overflow affordance.

Rating: 6/10

